#!/bin/bash
# Stands in for omarchy-menu-select while omarchy-menu-keybindings runs (see
# bin/omarchy-keybindings-de): shows the list with German key names and hands
# the original line back, so the script still finds and runs the binding.

shim_dir=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
PATH=$(tr ':' '\n' <<<"$PATH" | grep -vxF "$shim_dir" | paste -sd:)

prompt=$1
shift
[[ $prompt == Keybindings ]] && prompt=Tastenkürzel

catalog=$(mktemp)
trap 'rm -f "$catalog"' EXIT
jq -r '.exact | to_entries[] | "\(.key)\t\(.value)"' "$shim_dir/../../catalog/keybindings.json" >"$catalog" 2>/dev/null

mapfile -t originals
mapfile -t translated < <(printf '%s\n' "${originals[@]}" | awk -v catalog="$catalog" -f "$shim_dir/keys.awk")

declare -A original_of
shown=()
for i in "${!translated[@]}"; do
  [[ -z ${translated[$i]} ]] && continue
  original_of["${translated[$i]}"]=${originals[$i]}
  shown+=("${translated[$i]}")
done

selection=$(printf '%s\n' "${shown[@]}" | omarchy-menu-select "$prompt" "$@") || exit
[[ -n $selection ]] && printf '%s\n' "${original_of[$selection]:-$selection}"
